<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Definitions and Notations</h2>

<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>LLM Architecture</h3>

<section id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Weights</h4>

<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Here we provide notations for the rest of model A’s weights. In addition to the notations in <a href="#S3" title="3 Preliminary ‣ AWM: Accurate Weight-Matrix Fingerprint for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section 3</span></a>, we further denote s, <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{A,\text{lm}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext>lm</mtext></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{A,\text{lm}}</annotation></semantics></math> as the language model head, and <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{A,\text{V}}^{(l)},W_{A,\text{O}}^{(l)},\mathbb{W}_{A,\text{ffn}}^{(l)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext>V</mtext></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext>O</mtext></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝕎</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext>ffn</mtext></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{A,\text{V}}^{(l)},W_{A,\text{O}}^{(l)},\mathbb{W}_{A,\text{ffn}}^{(l)}</annotation></semantics></math> the V,O matrices and FFN at the <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>l</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l</annotation></semantics></math>-th layer,
and</p>
<table id="A1.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex1"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{W}_{A,\text{others}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝕎</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext>others</mtext></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{W}_{A,\text{others}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{W}_{A}/\mathbb{W}_{A,\text{partial}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝕎</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>𝕎</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext>partial</mtext></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{W}_{A}/\mathbb{W}_{A,\text{partial}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex2"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\{W_{A,\text{lm}}\}\bigcup_{l=1}^{L}\mathbb{W}_{A,\text{ffn}}^{(l)}\bigcup_{l=1}^{L}\{W_{A,i}^{(l)}\mid i\in\{\text{V},\text{O}\}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext>lm</mtext></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">⋃</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>L</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝕎</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext>ffn</mtext></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">⋃</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>L</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mtext>V</mtext><mo>,</mo><mtext>O</mtext><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\{W_{A,\text{lm}}\}\bigcup_{l=1}^{L}\mathbb{W}_{A,\text{ffn}}^{(l)}\bigcup_{l=1}^{L}\{W_{A,i}^{(l)}\mid i\in\{\text{V},\text{O}\}\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">as the rest of model A’s weights.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Functions</h4>

<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Here we provide definitions for functions in an LLM.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition A.1</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(RMSNorm)<span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Given the input matrix <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X\in\mathbb{R}^{m\times n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X\in\mathbb{R}^{m\times n}</annotation></semantics></math> of model A, the learnable parameters <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega_{A}^{(l)}=(\omega_{A,1}^{(l)},\dots,\omega_{A,n}^{(l)})\in\mathbb{R}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>ω</mi><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega_{A}^{(l)}=(\omega_{A,1}^{(l)},\dots,\omega_{A,n}^{(l)})\in\mathbb{R}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> at the <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>l</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l</annotation></semantics></math>-th layer, and a constant <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon_{A}\in\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon_{A}\in\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> (this constant is usually shared across all layers of an LLM), RMSNorm at layer <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>l</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l</annotation></semantics></math> is a function that</span></p>
<table id="A1.E6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{RMSNorm}(X,\omega_{A}^{(l)},\epsilon_{A})=\text{diag}^{-\frac{1}{2}}(XX^{\top}\mathbf{1}_{m}+\epsilon_{A}\mathbf{1}_{m})\cdot X\cdot\text{diag}(\omega_{A}^{(l)})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">RMSNorm</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>ω</mi><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">diag</mtext><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">diag</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>ω</mi><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{RMSNorm}(X,\omega_{A}^{(l)},\epsilon_{A})=\text{diag}^{-\frac{1}{2}}(XX^{\top}\mathbf{1}_{m}+\epsilon_{A}\mathbf{1}_{m})\cdot X\cdot\text{diag}(\omega_{A}^{(l)}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(6)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition A.2</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Self-Attention with RoPE)<span id="A1.Thmtheorem2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Given an input <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> to model A, the self-attention mechanism at layer <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>l</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l</annotation></semantics></math> is a function <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\text{attn}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">attn</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\text{attn}}</annotation></semantics></math> that</span></p>
<table id="A1.E7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\text{attn}}^{(l)}(X)=\text{AttnScore}(X,W_{A,\text{Q}}^{(l)},W_{A,\text{K}}^{(l)},\theta)\cdot XW_{A,\text{V}}^{(l)\top}\cdot W_{A,\text{O}}^{(l)\top}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">attn</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">AttnScore</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">Q</mtext></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">K</mtext></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">V</mtext></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em">⊤</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">O</mtext></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em">⊤</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\text{attn}}^{(l)}(X)=\text{AttnScore}(X,W_{A,\text{Q}}^{(l)},W_{A,\text{K}}^{(l)},\theta)\cdot XW_{A,\text{V}}^{(l)\top}\cdot W_{A,\text{O}}^{(l)\top}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where AttnScore is the attention score function with RoPE, i.e.</span></p>
<table id="A1.E8" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody><tr id="A1.EGx4" class="ltx_eqn_row"><td class="ltx_eqn_cell" colspan="5"></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E8.1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E8.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\text{AttnScore}(X,W_{A,\text{Q}}^{(l)},W_{A,\text{K}}^{(l)},\theta)=\text{softmax}\Big(\frac{1}{\sqrt{d}}\text{RoPE}(XW_{A,\text{Q}}^{(l)\top},\theta)\cdot\text{RoPE}(XW_{A,\text{K}}^{(l)\top},\theta)^{\top}\Big)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">AttnScore</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">Q</mtext></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">K</mtext></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">softmax</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mi>d</mi></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">RoPE</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">Q</mtext></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em">⊤</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">RoPE</mtext></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">K</mtext></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em">⊤</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{AttnScore}(X,W_{A,\text{Q}}^{(l)},W_{A,\text{K}}^{(l)},\theta)=\text{softmax}\Big(\frac{1}{\sqrt{d}}\text{RoPE}(XW_{A,\text{Q}}^{(l)\top},\theta)\cdot\text{RoPE}(XW_{A,\text{K}}^{(l)\top},\theta)^{\top}\Big),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(8a)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E8.2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E8.2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\text{RoPE}(XW_{A,\text{Q}}^{(l)\top},\theta)=[x_{1}^{\top}W_{A,\text{Q}}^{(l)\top}R_{\theta}(0),\dots,x_{m}^{\top}W_{A,\text{Q}}^{(l)\top}R_{\theta}(m-1)]," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">RoPE</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">Q</mtext></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em">⊤</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">Q</mtext></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em">⊤</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>m</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">Q</mtext></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em">⊤</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{RoPE}(XW_{A,\text{Q}}^{(l)\top},\theta)=[x_{1}^{\top}W_{A,\text{Q}}^{(l)\top}R_{\theta}(0),\dots,x_{m}^{\top}W_{A,\text{Q}}^{(l)\top}R_{\theta}(m-1)],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(8b)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E8.3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E8.3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\text{RoPE}(XW_{A,\text{K}}^{(l)\top},\theta)=[x_{1}^{\top}W_{A,\text{K}}^{(l)\top}R_{\theta}(0),\dots,x_{m}^{\top}W_{A,\text{K}}^{(l)\top}R_{\theta}(m-1)]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">RoPE</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">K</mtext></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em">⊤</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">K</mtext></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em">⊤</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>m</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">K</mtext></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em">⊤</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{RoPE}(XW_{A,\text{K}}^{(l)\top},\theta)=[x_{1}^{\top}W_{A,\text{K}}^{(l)\top}R_{\theta}(0),\dots,x_{m}^{\top}W_{A,\text{K}}^{(l)\top}R_{\theta}(m-1)].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(8c)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Here <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}^{\top}\in\mathbb{R}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}^{\top}\in\mathbb{R}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> is the i-th row of <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math> is the frequency base for RoPE and <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> is the rotation matrix <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib37" title="" class="ltx_ref">Su et al., 2024</a>)</cite>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">RoPE’s definition in <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem2" title="Definition A.2 (Self-Attention with RoPE). ‣ Functions ‣ A.1 LLM Architecture ‣ Appendix A Definitions and Notations ‣ AWM: Accurate Weight-Matrix Fingerprint for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Definition A.2</span></a> is slightly different from their implementations, but still an equivalent version to <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib37" title="" class="ltx_ref">Su et al. (2024)</a></cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition A.3</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Feed-forward Networks)<span id="A1.Thmtheorem3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Given the input <math id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math>, the feed-forward network which adopts the SwiGLU MLP is the function <math id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{(l)}_{\text{ffn}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">ffn</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{(l)}_{\text{ffn}}</annotation></semantics></math> defined by</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex1a" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex1a.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{(l)}_{\text{ffn}}(X)\;=\;\Big(\text{SiLU}\big(X\,{W^{(l)\top}_{A,\text{gate}}}\big)\odot\big(X\,{W^{(l)\top}_{A,\text{up}}}\big)\Big)\;{W^{(l)\top}_{A,\text{down}}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">ffn</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">SiLU</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">gate</mtext></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em">⊤</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">up</mtext></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em">⊤</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.280em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">down</mtext></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em">⊤</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{(l)}_{\text{ffn}}(X)\;=\;\Big(\text{SiLU}\big(X\,{W^{(l)\top}_{A,\text{gate}}}\big)\odot\big(X\,{W^{(l)\top}_{A,\text{up}}}\big)\Big)\;{W^{(l)\top}_{A,\text{down}}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W^{(l)}_{A,\text{up}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">up</mtext></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W^{(l)}_{A,\text{up}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W^{(l)}_{A,\text{gate}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">gate</mtext></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W^{(l)}_{A,\text{gate}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W^{(l)}_{A,\text{down}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">down</mtext></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W^{(l)}_{A,\text{down}}</annotation></semantics></math> are bias-free weight matrices, <math id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\odot" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊙</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\odot</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the Hadamard product, and <math id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{SiLU}(z)=z\,\sigma(z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">SiLU</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{SiLU}(z)=z\,\sigma(z)</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma(z)=\frac{1}{1+e^{-z}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma(z)=\frac{1}{1+e^{-z}}</annotation></semantics></math>. We write
<math id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{W}^{(l)}_{A,\text{ffn}}=\big\{W^{(l)}_{A,\text{up}},\,W^{(l)}_{A,\text{gate}},\,W^{(l)}_{A,\text{down}}\big\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝕎</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">ffn</mtext></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">up</mtext></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">gate</mtext></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">down</mtext></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{W}^{(l)}_{A,\text{ffn}}=\big\{W^{(l)}_{A,\text{up}},\,W^{(l)}_{A,\text{gate}},\,W^{(l)}_{A,\text{down}}\big\}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">We abuse the notations in <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem1" title="Definition A.1 (RMSNorm). ‣ Functions ‣ A.1 LLM Architecture ‣ Appendix A Definitions and Notations ‣ AWM: Accurate Weight-Matrix Fingerprint for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Definition A.1</span></a> by denoting <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{RMSNorm}_{\text{attn}}^{(l)}(X)\triangleq\text{RMSNorm}(X,\omega_{A,\text{attn}}^{(l)},\epsilon_{A})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mtext>RMSNorm</mtext><mtext>attn</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≜</mo><mrow><mtext>RMSNorm</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext>attn</mtext></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{RMSNorm}_{\text{attn}}^{(l)}(X)\triangleq\text{RMSNorm}(X,\omega_{A,\text{attn}}^{(l)},\epsilon_{A})</annotation></semantics></math> as the attention norm and <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{RMSNorm}_{\text{ffn}}^{(l)}(X)\triangleq\text{RMSNorm}(X,\omega_{A,\text{ffn}}^{(l)},\epsilon_{A})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mtext>RMSNorm</mtext><mtext>ffn</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≜</mo><mrow><mtext>RMSNorm</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext>ffn</mtext></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{RMSNorm}_{\text{ffn}}^{(l)}(X)\triangleq\text{RMSNorm}(X,\omega_{A,\text{ffn}}^{(l)},\epsilon_{A})</annotation></semantics></math> the ffn norm at layer <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>l</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l</annotation></semantics></math> of model A. Then, the definition of a Transformer block at layer <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>l</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l</annotation></semantics></math> of model A can be summartized as follows.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition A.4</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Transformer Block)<span id="A1.Thmtheorem4.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Combining all the components with residual connections, the transformer block at the <math id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>l</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l</annotation></semantics></math>-th layer of model A is a function <math id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\text{Transformer}}^{(l)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">Transformer</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\text{Transformer}}^{(l)}</annotation></semantics></math> that</span></p>
<table id="A1.E9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\text{Transformer}}^{(l)}=\Big(\text{I}+f_{\text{ffn}}^{(l)}\circ\text{RMSNorm}^{(l)}_{\text{ffn}}\Big)\circ\Big(\text{I}+f_{\text{attn}}^{(l)}\circ\text{RMSNorm}^{(l)}_{\text{attn}}\Big)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">Transformer</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">I</mtext><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">ffn</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msubsup><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">RMSNorm</mtext><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">ffn</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">I</mtext><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">attn</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msubsup><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">RMSNorm</mtext><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">attn</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\text{Transformer}}^{(l)}=\Big(\text{I}+f_{\text{ffn}}^{(l)}\circ\text{RMSNorm}^{(l)}_{\text{ffn}}\Big)\circ\Big(\text{I}+f_{\text{attn}}^{(l)}\circ\text{RMSNorm}^{(l)}_{\text{attn}}\Big).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(9)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <span id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath">I</span> is the identity mapping, <math id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\text{attn}}^{(l)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">attn</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\text{attn}}^{(l)}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\text{ffn}}^{(l)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">ffn</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\text{ffn}}^{(l)}</annotation></semantics></math> are the attention and FFN at <math id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>l</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l</annotation></semantics></math>-th layer respectively, <math id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{RMSNorm}^{(l)}_{\text{ffn}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">RMSNorm</mtext><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">ffn</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{RMSNorm}^{(l)}_{\text{ffn}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{RMSNorm}^{(l)}_{\text{attn}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">RMSNorm</mtext><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">attn</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{RMSNorm}^{(l)}_{\text{attn}}</annotation></semantics></math> are RMSNorm functions for these two components.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition A.5</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(LLM Architecture)<span id="A1.Thmtheorem5.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Given an word embedding <math id="A1.Thmtheorem5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math>, the last hidden state <math id="A1.Thmtheorem5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y</annotation></semantics></math> of an <math id="A1.Thmtheorem5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math>-layered LLM A is</span></p>
<table id="A1.E10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y=f_{\text{Transformer}}^{(L)}\circ f_{\text{Transformer}}^{(L-1)}\circ\dots\circ f_{\text{Transformer}}^{(L-1)}(X)\cdot W_{A,\text{lm}}^{\top}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">Transformer</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">Transformer</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">⋯</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">Transformer</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">lm</mtext></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y=f_{\text{Transformer}}^{(L)}\circ f_{\text{Transformer}}^{(L-1)}\circ\dots\circ f_{\text{Transformer}}^{(L-1)}(X)\cdot W_{A,\text{lm}}^{\top}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(10)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2 </span>Central Kernel Alignment (CKA)</h3>

<div id="A1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Given two input matrices <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{1}\in\mathbb{R}^{m\times n_{1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{1}\in\mathbb{R}^{m\times n_{1}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{2}\in\mathbb{R}^{m\times n_{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{2}\in\mathbb{R}^{m\times n_{2}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <span id="A1.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath">CKA</span> is a function mapping paired input matrices to <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>, and</p>
<table id="A1.E11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{CKA}(X_{1},X_{2})=\frac{\text{HSIC}(K_{X_{1}},K_{X_{2}})}{\sqrt{\text{HSIC}(K_{X_{1}},K_{X_{1}})\cdot\text{HSIC}(K_{X_{2}},K_{X_{2}})}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext>CKA</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mtext>HSIC</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msqrt><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>HSIC</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mtext>HSIC</mtext></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{CKA}(X_{1},X_{2})=\frac{\text{HSIC}(K_{X_{1}},K_{X_{2}})}{\sqrt{\text{HSIC}(K_{X_{1}},K_{X_{1}})\cdot\text{HSIC}(K_{X_{2}},K_{X_{2}})}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(11)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{HSIC}(K_{X_{1}},K_{X_{2}})=\frac{1}{(m-1)^{2}}\text{tr}(K_{X_{1}}H_{m}K_{X_{2}}H_{m})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext>HSIC</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>tr</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{HSIC}(K_{X_{1}},K_{X_{2}})=\frac{1}{(m-1)^{2}}\text{tr}(K_{X_{1}}H_{m}K_{X_{2}}H_{m})</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(K_{X_{1}})_{ij}=k((X_{1})_{i},(X_{1})_{j})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(K_{X_{1}})_{ij}=k((X_{1})_{i},(X_{1})_{j})</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(K_{X_{2}})_{ij}=k((X_{2})_{i},(X_{2})_{j})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(K_{X_{2}})_{ij}=k((X_{2})_{i},(X_{2})_{j})</annotation></semantics></math> are kernel matrices with the kernel function <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k(\cdot,\cdot):\mathbb{R}^{m}\times\mathbb{R}^{m}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}_{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>m</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>m</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>ℝ</mi><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k(\cdot,\cdot):\mathbb{R}^{m}\times\mathbb{R}^{m}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}_{+}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{m}=I_{m}-\frac{1}{m}\mathrm{1_{m}}\mathrm{1_{m}}^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>m</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn>1</mn><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mmultiscripts><mn>1</mn><mi>m</mi><mrow></mrow><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></mmultiscripts></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{m}=I_{m}-\frac{1}{m}\mathrm{1_{m}}\mathrm{1_{m}}^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math> is the centering matrix. The linear kernels give <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{X}=XX^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{X}=XX^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math> for a matrix <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math>.
To reduce the finite-sample bias of Eq. (6), we use the unbiased HSIC estimator <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib36" title="" class="ltx_ref">Song et al., 2007</a>)</cite>.
Let <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{K}_{X_{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{K}_{X_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math> be <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{X_{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>K</mi><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{X_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math> with its diagonal set to zero, i.e., <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\tilde{K}_{X_{i}})_{ii}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\tilde{K}_{X_{i}})_{ii}=0</annotation></semantics></math>.
With <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{1}_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mn>1</mn><mi>m</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{1}_{m}</annotation></semantics></math> the all-ones vector of length <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math>, the unbiased HSIC is</p>
<table id="A1.E12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center">
<div id="A1.E12.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_markedasmath ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:345.0pt;height:9.699999999999999pt;vertical-align:-2.5pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(-31.8pt,0.9pt) scale(0.844441551197933,0.844441551197933) ;">
<p id="A1.E12.2.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.E12.m1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{HSIC}_{u}(\tilde{K}_{X_{1}},\tilde{K}_{X_{2}})=\frac{1}{m(m-3)}\!\left[\mathrm{tr}(\tilde{K}_{X_{1}}\tilde{K}_{X_{2}})+\frac{(\mathrm{1}_{m}^{\top}\tilde{K}_{X_{1}}\mathrm{1}_{m})(\mathrm{1}_{m}^{\top}\tilde{K}_{X_{2}}\mathrm{1}_{m})}{(m-1)(m-2)}-\frac{2}{m-2}\,\mathrm{1}_{m}^{\top}\tilde{K}_{X_{1}}\tilde{K}_{X_{2}}\mathrm{1}_{m}\right]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mtext>HSIC</mtext><mi>u</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mn>1</mn><mi>m</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn>1</mn><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mn>1</mn><mi>m</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn>1</mn><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mn> 1</mn><mi>m</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn>1</mn><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{HSIC}_{u}(\tilde{K}_{X_{1}},\tilde{K}_{X_{2}})=\frac{1}{m(m-3)}\!\left[\mathrm{tr}(\tilde{K}_{X_{1}}\tilde{K}_{X_{2}})+\frac{(\mathrm{1}_{m}^{\top}\tilde{K}_{X_{1}}\mathrm{1}_{m})(\mathrm{1}_{m}^{\top}\tilde{K}_{X_{2}}\mathrm{1}_{m})}{(m-1)(m-2)}-\frac{2}{m-2}\,\mathrm{1}_{m}^{\top}\tilde{K}_{X_{1}}\tilde{K}_{X_{2}}\mathrm{1}_{m}\right].</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</span></div></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="0" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(12)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">We then define</p>
<table id="A1.E13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{UCKA}(X_{1},X_{2})=\frac{\text{HSIC}_{u}(\tilde{K}_{X_{1}},\tilde{K}_{X_{2}})}{\sqrt{\text{HSIC}_{u}(\tilde{K}_{X_{1}},\tilde{K}_{X_{1}})\cdot\text{HSIC}_{u}(\tilde{K}_{X_{2}},\tilde{K}_{X_{2}})}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>UCKA</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mtext>HSIC</mtext><mi>u</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msqrt><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mtext>HSIC</mtext><mi>u</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mtext>HSIC</mtext><mi>u</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mfrac></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{UCKA}(X_{1},X_{2})=\frac{\text{HSIC}_{u}(\tilde{K}_{X_{1}},\tilde{K}_{X_{2}})}{\sqrt{\text{HSIC}_{u}(\tilde{K}_{X_{1}},\tilde{K}_{X_{1}})\cdot\text{HSIC}_{u}(\tilde{K}_{X_{2}},\tilde{K}_{X_{2}})}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(13)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.4" class="ltx_p">which preserves <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 3.1. ‣ Central Kernel Alignment (CKA) ‣ 3 Preliminary ‣ AWM: Accurate Weight-Matrix Fingerprint for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem 3.1</span></a> and yields values in <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[-1,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[-1,1]</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Proofs and Discussions</h2>

<section id="A2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.1 </span>Proof for <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 3.1. ‣ Central Kernel Alignment (CKA) ‣ 3 Preliminary ‣ AWM: Accurate Weight-Matrix Fingerprint for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem 3.1</span></a></h3>

<div id="A2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We give the proof based on the definition of CKA with linear kernels in <a href="#A1.SS2" title="A.2 Central Kernel Alignment (CKA) ‣ Appendix A Definitions and Notations ‣ AWM: Accurate Weight-Matrix Fingerprint for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref">Appendix <span class="ltx_ref ltx_nolink"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.2</span></span></a>. Given input matrices <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{1},X_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{1},X_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, orthogonal matrices <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{1},U_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{1},U_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> and constants <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{1},c_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{1},c_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, the kernel functions yield</p>
<table id="A2.EGx5" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex2"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle K_{c_{1}X_{1}U_{1}}=c_{1}X_{1}U_{1}U_{1}^{\top}X_{1}^{\top}c_{1}=c_{1}^{2}X_{1}X_{1}^{\top}=c_{1}^{2}K_{X_{1}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle K_{c_{1}X_{1}U_{1}}=c_{1}X_{1}U_{1}U_{1}^{\top}X_{1}^{\top}c_{1}=c_{1}^{2}X_{1}X_{1}^{\top}=c_{1}^{2}K_{X_{1}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex3"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle K_{c_{2}X_{2}U_{2}}=c_{2}X_{2}U_{2}U_{2}^{\top}X_{2}^{\top}c_{2}=c_{2}^{2}X_{2}X_{2}^{\top}=c_{2}^{2}K_{X_{2}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle K_{c_{2}X_{2}U_{2}}=c_{2}X_{2}U_{2}U_{2}^{\top}X_{2}^{\top}c_{2}=c_{2}^{2}X_{2}X_{2}^{\top}=c_{2}^{2}K_{X_{2}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Therefore, corresponding HSIC results are</p>
<table id="A2.EGx6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\text{HSIC}(K_{c_{1}X_{1}U_{1}},K_{c_{2}X_{2}U_{2}})=\frac{c_{1}^{2}c_{2}^{2}}{(m-1)^{2}}\text{tr}(K_{X_{1}}H_{m}K_{X_{2}}H_{m})=c_{1}^{2}c_{2}^{2}\text{HSIC}(K_{X_{1}},K_{X_{2}})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>HSIC</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>tr</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>HSIC</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{HSIC}(K_{c_{1}X_{1}U_{1}},K_{c_{2}X_{2}U_{2}})=\frac{c_{1}^{2}c_{2}^{2}}{(m-1)^{2}}\text{tr}(K_{X_{1}}H_{m}K_{X_{2}}H_{m})=c_{1}^{2}c_{2}^{2}\text{HSIC}(K_{X_{1}},K_{X_{2}}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex5"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\text{HSIC}(K_{c_{1}X_{1}U_{1}},K_{c_{1}X_{1}U_{1}})=\frac{c_{1}^{4}}{(m-1)^{2}}\text{tr}(K_{X_{1}}H_{m}K_{X_{1}}H_{m})=c_{1}^{4}\text{HSIC}(K_{X_{1}},K_{X_{1}})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>HSIC</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></msubsup><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>tr</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>HSIC</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{HSIC}(K_{c_{1}X_{1}U_{1}},K_{c_{1}X_{1}U_{1}})=\frac{c_{1}^{4}}{(m-1)^{2}}\text{tr}(K_{X_{1}}H_{m}K_{X_{1}}H_{m})=c_{1}^{4}\text{HSIC}(K_{X_{1}},K_{X_{1}}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex6"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\text{HSIC}(K_{c_{2}X_{2}U_{2}},K_{c_{2}X_{2}U_{2}})=\frac{c_{2}^{4}}{(m-1)^{2}}\text{tr}(K_{X_{2}}H_{m}K_{X_{2}}H_{m})=c_{2}^{4}\text{HSIC}(K_{X_{2}},K_{X_{2}})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>HSIC</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>4</mn></msubsup><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>tr</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>4</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>HSIC</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{HSIC}(K_{c_{2}X_{2}U_{2}},K_{c_{2}X_{2}U_{2}})=\frac{c_{2}^{4}}{(m-1)^{2}}\text{tr}(K_{X_{2}}H_{m}K_{X_{2}}H_{m})=c_{2}^{4}\text{HSIC}(K_{X_{2}},K_{X_{2}}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Hence, it follows that</p>
<table id="A2.EGx7" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\text{CKA}(c_{1}X_{1}U_{1},c_{2}X_{2}U_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>CKA</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{CKA}(c_{1}X_{1}U_{1},c_{2}X_{2}U_{2})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\text{HSIC}(K_{c_{1}X_{1}U_{1}},K_{c_{2}X_{2}U_{2}})}{\sqrt{\text{HSIC}(K_{c_{1}X_{1}U_{1}},K_{c_{1}X_{1}U_{1}})\cdot\text{HSIC}(K_{c_{2}X_{2}U_{2}},K_{c_{2}X_{2}U_{2}})}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mtext>HSIC</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msqrt><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>HSIC</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mtext>HSIC</mtext></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\text{HSIC}(K_{c_{1}X_{1}U_{1}},K_{c_{2}X_{2}U_{2}})}{\sqrt{\text{HSIC}(K_{c_{1}X_{1}U_{1}},K_{c_{1}X_{1}U_{1}})\cdot\text{HSIC}(K_{c_{2}X_{2}U_{2}},K_{c_{2}X_{2}U_{2}})}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex8"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{c_{1}^{2}c_{2}^{2}\text{HSIC}(K_{X_{1}},K_{X_{2}})}{c_{1}^{2}c_{2}^{2}\sqrt{\text{HSIC}(K_{X_{1}},K_{X_{1}})\cdot\text{HSIC}(K_{X_{2}},K_{X_{2}})}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>HSIC</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>HSIC</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mtext>HSIC</mtext></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{c_{1}^{2}c_{2}^{2}\text{HSIC}(K_{X_{1}},K_{X_{2}})}{c_{1}^{2}c_{2}^{2}\sqrt{\text{HSIC}(K_{X_{1}},K_{X_{1}})\cdot\text{HSIC}(K_{X_{2}},K_{X_{2}})}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex9"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\text{HSIC}(K_{X_{1}},K_{X_{2}})}{\sqrt{\text{HSIC}(K_{X_{1}},K_{X_{1}})\cdot\text{HSIC}(K_{X_{2}},K_{X_{2}})}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mtext>HSIC</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msqrt><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>HSIC</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mtext>HSIC</mtext></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\text{HSIC}(K_{X_{1}},K_{X_{2}})}{\sqrt{\text{HSIC}(K_{X_{1}},K_{X_{1}})\cdot\text{HSIC}(K_{X_{2}},K_{X_{2}})}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex10"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\text{CKA}(X_{1},X_{2})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>CKA</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\text{CKA}(X_{1},X_{2}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.2 </span>Proof for <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem2" title="Proposition 4.2 (Proof in Appendix ). ‣ 4.2 Residual Connections: Passing Manipulations Forward ‣ 4 Manipulations on An Open-Source LLM ‣ AWM: Accurate Weight-Matrix Fingerprint for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Proposition 4.2</span></a></h3>

<div id="A2.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The goal is to show the manipulation <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> commutes with <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e. <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f\circ T=T\circ f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f\circ T=T\circ f</annotation></semantics></math>. If <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f=f_{n}\circ\dots\circ f_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">⋯</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f=f_{n}\circ\dots\circ f_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, then it suffices to show</p>
<table id="A2.Ex11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{n}\circ\dots\circ f_{1}\circ T=T\circ f_{n}\circ\dots f_{1}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">⋯</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{n}\circ\dots\circ f_{1}\circ T=T\circ f_{n}\circ\dots f_{1}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Since</p>
<table id="A2.Ex12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="f_{1}\circ T=T\circ f_{1},f_{2}\circ T=T\circ f_{2},\dots,f_{n}\circ T=T\circ f_{n}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>f</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>f</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>f</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>f</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>f</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{1}\circ T=T\circ f_{1},f_{2}\circ T=T\circ f_{2},\dots,f_{n}\circ T=T\circ f_{n},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">It is direct that</p>
<table id="A2.Ex13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f\circ T=T\circ f." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f\circ T=T\circ f.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.3 </span>Proof for <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem 4.3. ‣ 4.3 RMSNorm: A Constraint on Embedding Manipulations ‣ 4 Manipulations on An Open-Source LLM ‣ AWM: Accurate Weight-Matrix Fingerprint for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem 4.3</span></a> and Discussions on Other Input Manipulations</h3>

<div id="A2.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">We first show a proof for the claims in <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem 4.3. ‣ 4.3 RMSNorm: A Constraint on Embedding Manipulations ‣ 4 Manipulations on An Open-Source LLM ‣ AWM: Accurate Weight-Matrix Fingerprint for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem 4.3</span></a>.</span> The core lies in preserving the diagonal structure of RMSNorm parameters in <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem1" title="Definition A.1 (RMSNorm). ‣ Functions ‣ A.1 LLM Architecture ‣ Appendix A Definitions and Notations ‣ AWM: Accurate Weight-Matrix Fingerprint for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Definition A.1</span></a>. Given the input <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> to layer <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>l</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l</annotation></semantics></math>, the manipulations change it to <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="cXPD" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">cXPD</annotation></semantics></math> and fed the manipulated input into the attention norm of model B. In order to recover the manipulations on inputs after RMSNorm, i.e. for any manipulation <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> in the input <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> (an example is <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T(X)=cXPD" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T(X)=cXPD</annotation></semantics></math>),</p>
<table id="A2.E14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{RMSNorm}_{\text{attn}}^{(l)}\circ T=T\circ\text{RMSNorm}_{\text{attn}}^{(l)}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mtext>RMSNorm</mtext><mtext>attn</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msubsup><mtext>RMSNorm</mtext><mtext>attn</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{RMSNorm}_{\text{attn}}^{(l)}\circ T=T\circ\text{RMSNorm}_{\text{attn}}^{(l)},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(14)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">it suffices to show</p>
<table id="A2.Ex14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\exists\omega_{B,\text{attn}}^{(l)}\text{ and }\epsilon_{B}\text{, s.t. }\text{RMSNorm}(X,\omega_{A,\text{attn}}^{(l)},\epsilon_{A})\cdot cPD=\text{RMSNorm}(cXPD,\omega_{B,\text{attn}}^{(l)},\epsilon_{B})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∃</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext>attn</mtext></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> and </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mtext>, s.t. </mtext><mtext>RMSNorm</mtext></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext>attn</mtext></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>RMSNorm</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext>attn</mtext></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\exists\omega_{B,\text{attn}}^{(l)}\text{ and }\epsilon_{B}\text{, s.t. }\text{RMSNorm}(X,\omega_{A,\text{attn}}^{(l)},\epsilon_{A})\cdot cPD=\text{RMSNorm}(cXPD,\omega_{B,\text{attn}}^{(l)},\epsilon_{B})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p1.3" class="ltx_p">since the learnable parameters and norm epsilon can be modified to satisfy <a href="#A2.E14" title="Equation 14 ‣ B.3 Proof for and Discussions on Other Input Manipulations ‣ Appendix B Proofs and Discussions ‣ AWM: Accurate Weight-Matrix Fingerprint for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Equation 14</span></a> and <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem2" title="Proposition 4.2 (Proof in Appendix ). ‣ 4.2 Residual Connections: Passing Manipulations Forward ‣ 4 Manipulations on An Open-Source LLM ‣ AWM: Accurate Weight-Matrix Fingerprint for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Proposition 4.2</span></a>. By setting <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon_{B}=c^{2}\epsilon_{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon_{B}=c^{2}\epsilon_{A}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{diag}(\omega_{B,\text{attn}}^{(l)})=cD^{\top}P^{\top}\text{diag}(\omega_{A,\text{attn}}^{(l)})PD" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext>diag</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext>attn</mtext></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>diag</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext>attn</mtext></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{diag}(\omega_{B,\text{attn}}^{(l)})=cD^{\top}P^{\top}\text{diag}(\omega_{A,\text{attn}}^{(l)})PD</annotation></semantics></math>, one has</p>
<table id="A2.EGx8" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\text{RMSNorm}(cXPD,\omega_{B,\text{attn}}^{(l)},\epsilon_{B})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>RMSNorm</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext>attn</mtext></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{RMSNorm}(cXPD,\omega_{B,\text{attn}}^{(l)},\epsilon_{B})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex16"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\text{diag}^{-\frac{1}{2}}\left((cXPD)(cXPD)^{\top}\mathbf{1}_{m}+\epsilon_{B}\mathbf{1}_{m}\right)\cdot cXPD\cdot\text{diag}(\omega_{B,\text{attn}}^{(l)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mtext>diag</mtext><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mtext>diag</mtext></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext>attn</mtext></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\text{diag}^{-\frac{1}{2}}\left((cXPD)(cXPD)^{\top}\mathbf{1}_{m}+\epsilon_{B}\mathbf{1}_{m}\right)\cdot cXPD\cdot\text{diag}(\omega_{B,\text{attn}}^{(l)})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex17"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\text{diag}^{-\frac{1}{2}}(c^{2}XX^{\top}\mathbf{1}_{m}+c^{2}\epsilon_{A}\mathbf{1}_{m})\cdot cXPD\cdot cD^{\top}P^{\top}\text{diag}(\omega_{A,\text{attn}}^{(l)})PD" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mtext>diag</mtext><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>diag</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext>attn</mtext></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\text{diag}^{-\frac{1}{2}}(c^{2}XX^{\top}\mathbf{1}_{m}+c^{2}\epsilon_{A}\mathbf{1}_{m})\cdot cXPD\cdot cD^{\top}P^{\top}\text{diag}(\omega_{A,\text{attn}}^{(l)})PD</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex18"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=c\cdot\text{diag}^{-\frac{1}{2}}(XX^{\top}\mathbf{1}_{m}+\epsilon_{A}\mathbf{1}_{m})\cdot X\cdot\text{diag}(\omega_{A,\text{attn}}^{(l)})\cdot PD" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mtext>diag</mtext><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mtext>diag</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext>attn</mtext></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=c\cdot\text{diag}^{-\frac{1}{2}}(XX^{\top}\mathbf{1}_{m}+\epsilon_{A}\mathbf{1}_{m})\cdot X\cdot\text{diag}(\omega_{A,\text{attn}}^{(l)})\cdot PD</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex19"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\text{RMSNorm}(X,\omega_{A,\text{attn}}^{(l)})\cdot cPD." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>RMSNorm</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext>attn</mtext></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\text{RMSNorm}(X,\omega_{A,\text{attn}}^{(l)})\cdot cPD.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p1.4" class="ltx_p">The proof still holds for partial permutations <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e. <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> is rectangular with number of rows more than number of columns, since <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="cD^{\top}P^{\top}\text{diag}(\omega_{A,\text{attn}}^{(l)})PD" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>diag</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext>attn</mtext></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">cD^{\top}P^{\top}\text{diag}(\omega_{A,\text{attn}}^{(l)})PD</annotation></semantics></math> is still a diagonal matrix. Therefore, <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{B,\text{emb}}=cPD" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext>emb</mtext></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{B,\text{emb}}=cPD</annotation></semantics></math> under <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem2" title="Proposition 4.2 (Proof in Appendix ). ‣ 4.2 Residual Connections: Passing Manipulations Forward ‣ 4 Manipulations on An Open-Source LLM ‣ AWM: Accurate Weight-Matrix Fingerprint for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Proposition 4.2</span></a>. <span id="A2.SS3.p1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">However, for more general manipulations, <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem2" title="Proposition 4.2 (Proof in Appendix ). ‣ 4.2 Residual Connections: Passing Manipulations Forward ‣ 4 Manipulations on An Open-Source LLM ‣ AWM: Accurate Weight-Matrix Fingerprint for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Proposition 4.2</span></a> does not hold for RMSNorm.</span> We give two examples for illustration.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">First, <span id="A2.SS3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">orthogonal transformations on the input generally fail to pass through RMSNorm</span>. Given any orthogonal matrices <math id="A2.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math> as the manipulation on <math id="A2.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e., <math id="A2.SS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T(X)=XU" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T(X)=XU</annotation></semantics></math>, if one attempts to keep <a href="#A2.E14" title="Equation 14 ‣ B.3 Proof for and Discussions on Other Input Manipulations ‣ Appendix B Proofs and Discussions ‣ AWM: Accurate Weight-Matrix Fingerprint for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Equation 14</span></a>, then it requires</p>
<table id="A2.Ex20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\exists\omega^{(l)}\text{ and }\epsilon,\text{ s.t. }\text{RMSNorm}(XU,\omega^{(l)},\epsilon)=\text{RMSNorm}(X,\omega_{A,\text{attn}}^{(l)},\epsilon_{A})U." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∃</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> and </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext> s.t. </mtext><mtext>RMSNorm</mtext></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>RMSNorm</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext>attn</mtext></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\exists\omega^{(l)}\text{ and }\epsilon,\text{ s.t. }\text{RMSNorm}(XU,\omega^{(l)},\epsilon)=\text{RMSNorm}(X,\omega_{A,\text{attn}}^{(l)},\epsilon_{A})U.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p2.2" class="ltx_p">However,</p>
<table id="A2.Ex21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{RMSNorm}(XU,\omega,\epsilon)=\text{diag}^{-\frac{1}{2}}(XX^{\top}\mathbf{1}_{m}+\epsilon\mathbf{1}_{m})\cdot XU\cdot\text{diag}(\omega^{(l)})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>RMSNorm</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mtext>diag</mtext><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mtext>diag</mtext></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{RMSNorm}(XU,\omega,\epsilon)=\text{diag}^{-\frac{1}{2}}(XX^{\top}\mathbf{1}_{m}+\epsilon\mathbf{1}_{m})\cdot XU\cdot\text{diag}(\omega^{(l)}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p2.3" class="ltx_p">Hence, it is required that</p>
<table id="A2.Ex22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U\cdot\text{diag}(\omega^{(l)})=\text{diag}(\omega_{A,\text{attn}}^{(l)})U" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mtext>diag</mtext></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>diag</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext>attn</mtext></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U\cdot\text{diag}(\omega^{(l)})=\text{diag}(\omega_{A,\text{attn}}^{(l)})U</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p2.4" class="ltx_p">which suggests <math id="A2.SS3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U^{\top}\text{diag}(\omega_{A,\text{attn}}^{(l)})U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>U</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>diag</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext>attn</mtext></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U^{\top}\text{diag}(\omega_{A,\text{attn}}^{(l)})U</annotation></semantics></math> is a diagonal matrix. Nevertheless, this property generally does not hold if <math id="A2.SS3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math> is not a (partial) permutation matrix <math id="A2.SS3.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> or a signature matrix <math id="A2.SS3.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Second, non-orthogonal transformations on inputs generally fail to pass through RMSNorm.</span> Given an arbitrary (invertible) transformation <math id="A2.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math>, <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem2" title="Proposition 4.2 (Proof in Appendix ). ‣ 4.2 Residual Connections: Passing Manipulations Forward ‣ 4 Manipulations on An Open-Source LLM ‣ AWM: Accurate Weight-Matrix Fingerprint for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Proposition 4.2</span></a> and <a href="#A2.E14" title="Equation 14 ‣ B.3 Proof for and Discussions on Other Input Manipulations ‣ Appendix B Proofs and Discussions ‣ AWM: Accurate Weight-Matrix Fingerprint for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Equation 14</span></a> require that</p>
<table id="A2.Ex23" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\exists\omega^{(l)}\text{ and }\epsilon,\text{ s.t. }\text{RMSNorm}(XM,\omega^{(l)},\epsilon)=\text{RMSNorm}(X,\omega_{A,\text{attn}}^{(l)},\epsilon_{A})M." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∃</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> and </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext> s.t. </mtext><mtext>RMSNorm</mtext></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>RMSNorm</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext>attn</mtext></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\exists\omega^{(l)}\text{ and }\epsilon,\text{ s.t. }\text{RMSNorm}(XM,\omega^{(l)},\epsilon)=\text{RMSNorm}(X,\omega_{A,\text{attn}}^{(l)},\epsilon_{A})M.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p3.2" class="ltx_p">However, since</p>
<table id="A2.Ex24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{RMSNorm}(XM,\omega^{(l)},\epsilon)=\text{diag}^{-\frac{1}{2}}(XMM^{\top}X^{\top}\mathbf{1}_{m}+\epsilon\mathbf{1}_{m})\cdot XM\cdot\text{diag}(\omega^{(l)})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>RMSNorm</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mtext>diag</mtext><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mtext>diag</mtext></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{RMSNorm}(XM,\omega^{(l)},\epsilon)=\text{diag}^{-\frac{1}{2}}(XMM^{\top}X^{\top}\mathbf{1}_{m}+\epsilon\mathbf{1}_{m})\cdot XM\cdot\text{diag}(\omega^{(l)}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p3.3" class="ltx_p">any <math id="A2.SS3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> that do not satisfy <math id="A2.SS3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="MM^{\top}=c^{\prime}I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>c</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">MM^{\top}=c^{\prime}I</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="A2.SS3.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>c</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> is a constant and <math id="A2.SS3.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>I</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I</annotation></semantics></math> is the identity matrix can hardly recover the manipulations due to the nonlinearity in norm functions. Moreover, similar to the case with orthogonal transformations, <math id="A2.SS3.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M\cdot\text{diag}(\omega^{(l)})=\text{diag}(\omega_{A,\text{attn}}^{(l)})M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mtext>diag</mtext></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>diag</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext>attn</mtext></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M\cdot\text{diag}(\omega^{(l)})=\text{diag}(\omega_{A,\text{attn}}^{(l)})M</annotation></semantics></math> also requires <math id="A2.SS3.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> to be (partial) permutation or signature matrices (or a combination of the both).</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Third, we additionally clarify that although the combination of (partial) permutation and signature matrices can be in any order, it is reasonable to fix it as <math id="A2.SS3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{B,\text{emb}}=cPD" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">emb</mtext></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{B,\text{emb}}=cPD</annotation></semantics></math>.</span> To be specific, we clarify that for any (partial) permutation matrix <math id="A2.SS3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> and signature matrix <math id="A2.SS3.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>D</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, there exists a (partial) permutation matrix <math id="A2.SS3.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> and a signature <math id="A2.SS3.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math> such that</p>
<table id="A2.Ex25" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D^{\prime}P^{\prime}=PD" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>D</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D^{\prime}P^{\prime}=PD</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p4.2" class="ltx_p">The proof is straightforward.
Define <math id="A2.SS3.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> entry-wise by</p>
<table id="A2.Ex26" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{ij}:=\bigl|(D^{\prime}P^{\prime})_{ij}\bigr|\in\{0,1\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>D</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{ij}:=\bigl|(D^{\prime}P^{\prime})_{ij}\bigr|\in\{0,1\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p4.3" class="ltx_p">Since left-multiplication by <math id="A2.SS3.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>D</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> only flips signs, each column of <math id="A2.SS3.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D^{\prime}P^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>D</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D^{\prime}P^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> has at most one nonzero entry. Hence, <math id="A2.SS3.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> is a partial permutation matrix.
For each column <math id="A2.SS3.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math>, if that column of <math id="A2.SS3.p4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D^{\prime}P^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>D</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D^{\prime}P^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> has its unique nonzero at row <math id="A2.SS3.p4.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>, set</p>
<table id="A2.Ex27" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{jj}:=\operatorname{sgn}\bigl((D^{\prime}P^{\prime})_{ij}\bigr)\in\{\pm 1\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>sgn</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>D</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo>±</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{jj}:=\operatorname{sgn}\bigl((D^{\prime}P^{\prime})_{ij}\bigr)\in\{\pm 1\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p4.4" class="ltx_p">If the column is entirely zero, choose <math id="A2.SS3.p4.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{jj}\in\{\pm 1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo>±</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{jj}\in\{\pm 1\}</annotation></semantics></math> arbitrarily. Then for all <math id="A2.SS3.p4.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i,j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i,j</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A2.Ex28" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(PD)_{ij}=P_{ij}D_{jj}=\bigl|(D^{\prime}P^{\prime})_{ij}\bigr|\cdot\operatorname{sgn}\bigl((D^{\prime}P^{\prime})_{ij}\bigr)=(D^{\prime}P^{\prime})_{ij}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>D</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.055em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>sgn</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>D</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>D</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(PD)_{ij}=P_{ij}D_{jj}=\bigl|(D^{\prime}P^{\prime})_{ij}\bigr|\cdot\operatorname{sgn}\bigl((D^{\prime}P^{\prime})_{ij}\bigr)=(D^{\prime}P^{\prime})_{ij},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p4.5" class="ltx_p">where we interpret <math id="A2.SS3.p4.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{sgn}(0)=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>sgn</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{sgn}(0)=1</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore, <math id="A2.SS3.p4.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="PD=D^{\prime}P^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>D</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">PD=D^{\prime}P^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Last, we clarify that the conclusions in <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem 4.3. ‣ 4.3 RMSNorm: A Constraint on Embedding Manipulations ‣ 4 Manipulations on An Open-Source LLM ‣ AWM: Accurate Weight-Matrix Fingerprint for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem 4.3</span></a> can generalize to the case where model A and model B may not share the same architecture.</span> It is a direct result from the fact that the two LLMs have shared tokens and that the pruning over dimensions of a model’s word embeddings can be viewed as a partial permutation matrix.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.4 </span>Proof for <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem4" title="Theorem 4.4. ‣ 4.4 RoPE and Attention Scores: Boundaries for Q/K Manipulations ‣ 4 Manipulations on An Open-Source LLM ‣ AWM: Accurate Weight-Matrix Fingerprint for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem 4.4</span></a> and Related Discussions</h3>

<div id="A2.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">We first provide the proof for <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem4" title="Theorem 4.4. ‣ 4.4 RoPE and Attention Scores: Boundaries for Q/K Manipulations ‣ 4 Manipulations on An Open-Source LLM ‣ AWM: Accurate Weight-Matrix Fingerprint for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem 4.4</span></a> based on <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem2" title="Definition A.2 (Self-Attention with RoPE). ‣ Functions ‣ A.1 LLM Architecture ‣ Appendix A Definitions and Notations ‣ AWM: Accurate Weight-Matrix Fingerprint for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Definition A.2</span></a>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We denote by <math id="A2.SS4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> the original input to self-attention, and <math id="A2.SS4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> the manipulated one. Then, <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem 4.3. ‣ 4.3 RMSNorm: A Constraint on Embedding Manipulations ‣ 4 Manipulations on An Open-Source LLM ‣ AWM: Accurate Weight-Matrix Fingerprint for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem 4.3</span></a> suggests that</p>
<table id="A2.Ex29" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X^{\prime}=cXPD" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X^{\prime}=cXPD</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.p2.2" class="ltx_p">Therefore, the attention score of model B becomes</p>
<table id="A2.Ex30" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center">
<div id="A2.Ex30.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_markedasmath ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:345.0pt;height:12.8pt;vertical-align:-3.2pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(-42.5pt,1.6pt) scale(0.80234605254459,0.80234605254459) ;">
<p id="A2.Ex30.1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A2.Ex30.m1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{AttnScore}(cXPD,W_{B,\text{Q}}^{(l)},W_{B,\text{K}}^{(l)},\theta)=\text{softmax}\Big(\frac{1}{\sqrt{d}}\text{RoPE}(cXPDW_{B,\text{Q}}^{(l)\top},\theta)\cdot\text{RoPE}(cXPDW_{B,\text{K}}^{(l)\top},\theta)^{\top}\Big)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>AttnScore</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext>Q</mtext></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext>K</mtext></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>softmax</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mi>d</mi></msqrt></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>RoPE</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext>Q</mtext></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em">⊤</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mtext>RoPE</mtext></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext>K</mtext></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em">⊤</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{AttnScore}(cXPD,W_{B,\text{Q}}^{(l)},W_{B,\text{K}}^{(l)},\theta)=\text{softmax}\Big(\frac{1}{\sqrt{d}}\text{RoPE}(cXPDW_{B,\text{Q}}^{(l)\top},\theta)\cdot\text{RoPE}(cXPDW_{B,\text{K}}^{(l)\top},\theta)^{\top}\Big).</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</span></div></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.p2.3" class="ltx_p">To keep attention scores of model B identical to that of model A, it is required that</p>
<table id="A2.Ex31" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{RoPE}(cXPDW_{B,\text{Q}}^{(l)\top},\theta)\cdot\text{RoPE}(cXPDW_{B,\text{K}}^{(l)\top},\theta)^{\top}=\text{RoPE}(XW_{A,\text{Q}}^{(l)\top},\theta)\cdot\text{RoPE}(XW_{A,\text{K}}^{(l)\top})^{\top}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>RoPE</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext>Q</mtext></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em">⊤</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mtext>RoPE</mtext></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext>K</mtext></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em">⊤</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>RoPE</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext>Q</mtext></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em">⊤</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mtext>RoPE</mtext></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext>K</mtext></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em">⊤</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{RoPE}(cXPDW_{B,\text{Q}}^{(l)\top},\theta)\cdot\text{RoPE}(cXPDW_{B,\text{K}}^{(l)\top},\theta)^{\top}=\text{RoPE}(XW_{A,\text{Q}}^{(l)\top},\theta)\cdot\text{RoPE}(XW_{A,\text{K}}^{(l)\top})^{\top}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.p2.4" class="ltx_p">By <a href="#A1.E8.2" title="Equation 8b ‣ Equation 8 ‣ Definition A.2 (Self-Attention with RoPE). ‣ Functions ‣ A.1 LLM Architecture ‣ Appendix A Definitions and Notations ‣ AWM: Accurate Weight-Matrix Fingerprint for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Equation 8b</span></a> and <a href="#A1.E8.3" title="Equation 8c ‣ Equation 8 ‣ Definition A.2 (Self-Attention with RoPE). ‣ Functions ‣ A.1 LLM Architecture ‣ Appendix A Definitions and Notations ‣ AWM: Accurate Weight-Matrix Fingerprint for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Equation 8c</span></a>, this translates into</p>
<table id="A2.Ex32" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c^{2}x_{i}^{\top}PDW_{B,\text{Q}}^{(l)\top}R_{\theta}(i)R_{\theta}^{\top}(j)W_{B,\text{K}}^{(l)}D^{\top}P^{\top}x_{j}=x_{i}^{\top}W_{A,\text{Q}}^{(l)\top}R_{\theta}(i)R_{\theta}^{\top}(j)W_{A,K}^{(l)}x_{j}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext>Q</mtext></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em">⊤</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>θ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext>K</mtext></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext>Q</mtext></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em">⊤</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>θ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c^{2}x_{i}^{\top}PDW_{B,\text{Q}}^{(l)\top}R_{\theta}(i)R_{\theta}^{\top}(j)W_{B,\text{K}}^{(l)}D^{\top}P^{\top}x_{j}=x_{i}^{\top}W_{A,\text{Q}}^{(l)\top}R_{\theta}(i)R_{\theta}^{\top}(j)W_{A,K}^{(l)}x_{j}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.p2.5" class="ltx_p">Therefore, the recovery of model A’s attention score requires column-wise transformations to eliminate the <span id="A2.SS4.p2.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">input-related manipulations passed by RMSNorm</span>, i.e.</p>
<table id="A2.E15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{B,\text{Q}}^{(l)}=c^{-1}W_{A,\text{Q}}^{(l)}PD,\quad W_{B,\text{K}}^{(l)}=c^{-1}W_{A,\text{K}}^{(l)}PD" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext>Q</mtext></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>c</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext>Q</mtext></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext>K</mtext></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>c</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext>K</mtext></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{B,\text{Q}}^{(l)}=c^{-1}W_{A,\text{Q}}^{(l)}PD,\quad W_{B,\text{K}}^{(l)}=c^{-1}W_{A,\text{K}}^{(l)}PD</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(15)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.p2.6" class="ltx_p">which suggests</p>
<table id="A2.Ex33" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{B,\text{Q}}^{(l)}=R_{B,\text{K}}^{(l)}=c^{-1}PD." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext>Q</mtext></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext>K</mtext></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>c</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{B,\text{Q}}^{(l)}=R_{B,\text{K}}^{(l)}=c^{-1}PD.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.p2.7" class="ltx_p">Although <a href="#A2.E15" title="Equation 15 ‣ B.4 Proof for and Related Discussions ‣ Appendix B Proofs and Discussions ‣ AWM: Accurate Weight-Matrix Fingerprint for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Equation 15</span></a> recovers attention scores, the Q,K matrices can still be modified without changing attention scores. An example is, given a rotation matrix <math id="A2.SS4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R=R_{\theta}(k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R=R_{\theta}(k)</annotation></semantics></math> with the same frequency base as RoPE, multiplying Q,K matrices with it does not change the attention scores, i.e.</p>
<table id="A2.EGx9" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex34"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle x_{i}^{\top}W_{B,\text{Q}}^{(l)\top}R_{\theta}(k)R_{\theta}(i)R_{\theta}^{\top}(j)R_{\theta}^{\top}(k)W_{B,\text{K}}^{(l)}x_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext>Q</mtext></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em">⊤</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>θ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>θ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext>K</mtext></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle x_{i}^{\top}W_{B,\text{Q}}^{(l)\top}R_{\theta}(k)R_{\theta}(i)R_{\theta}^{\top}(j)R_{\theta}^{\top}(k)W_{B,\text{K}}^{(l)}x_{j}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex34.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=x_{i}^{\top}W_{B,\text{Q}}^{(l)\top}R_{\theta}(i+k)R_{\theta}^{\top}(j+k)W_{B,\text{K}}^{(l)\top}x_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext>Q</mtext></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em">⊤</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>θ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext>K</mtext></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em">⊤</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=x_{i}^{\top}W_{B,\text{Q}}^{(l)\top}R_{\theta}(i+k)R_{\theta}^{\top}(j+k)W_{B,\text{K}}^{(l)\top}x_{j}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex35"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=x_{i}^{\top}W_{B,\text{Q}}^{(l)\top}R_{\theta}(i-j)W_{B,\text{K}}^{(l)}x_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext>Q</mtext></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em">⊤</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext>K</mtext></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=x_{i}^{\top}W_{B,\text{Q}}^{(l)\top}R_{\theta}(i-j)W_{B,\text{K}}^{(l)}x_{j}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex36"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=x_{i}^{\top}W_{B,\text{Q}}^{(l)\top}R_{\theta}(i)R_{\theta}^{\top}(j)W_{B,\text{K}}^{(l)\top}x_{j}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext>Q</mtext></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em">⊤</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>θ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext>K</mtext></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em">⊤</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=x_{i}^{\top}W_{B,\text{Q}}^{(l)\top}R_{\theta}(i)R_{\theta}^{\top}(j)W_{B,\text{K}}^{(l)\top}x_{j}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.p2.8" class="ltx_p">Furthermore, this conclusion can be generalize to any rotation matrix with structures similar to RoPE rotation matrices.
Given <math id="A2.SS4.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R=\text{diag}(R(\psi_{0}),R(\psi_{1}),\dots)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>diag</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R=\text{diag}(R(\psi_{0}),R(\psi_{1}),\dots)</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A2.SS4.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R(\psi_{k})=\begin{bmatrix}\cos\psi_{k}&amp;-\sin\psi_{k}\\
\sin\psi_{k}&amp;\cos\psi_{k}\end{bmatrix}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R(\psi_{k})=\begin{bmatrix}\cos\psi_{k}&amp;-\sin\psi_{k}\\
\sin\psi_{k}&amp;\cos\psi_{k}\end{bmatrix}</annotation></semantics></math>, multiplying Q,K matrices by <math id="A2.SS4.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math> keeps the attention scores since</p>
<table id="A2.E16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="RR_{\theta}(i)R_{\theta}^{\top}(j)R^{\top}=R_{\theta}(i)R_{\theta}^{\top}(j)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>θ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>θ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">RR_{\theta}(i)R_{\theta}^{\top}(j)R^{\top}=R_{\theta}(i)R_{\theta}^{\top}(j).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(16)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.p2.9" class="ltx_p">Hence, there are various rotation matrices to significantly change Q,K matrices but preserve attention scores. Since these rotation matrices are naturally orthogonal, we reformulate the row-wise transformations on Q,K matrices <math id="A2.SS4.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{B,\text{Q}},L_{B,\text{K}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext>Q</mtext></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext>K</mtext></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{B,\text{Q}},L_{B,\text{K}}</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="A2.SS4.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{B,\text{Q}}^{(l)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext>Q</mtext></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{B,\text{Q}}^{(l)}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS4.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{B,\text{K}}^{(l)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext>K</mtext></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{B,\text{K}}^{(l)}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Therefore, we denote <span id="A2.SS4.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">RoPE-related manipulations as</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex37" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{B,\text{Q}}^{(l)}=U_{A,\text{Q}}^{(l)}W_{B,\text{Q}}^{(l)},\quad W_{B,\text{K}}^{(l)}=U_{A,\text{K}}^{(l)}W_{B,\text{K}}^{(l)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext>Q</mtext></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext>Q</mtext></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext>Q</mtext></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext>K</mtext></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext>K</mtext></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext>K</mtext></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{B,\text{Q}}^{(l)}=U_{A,\text{Q}}^{(l)}W_{B,\text{Q}}^{(l)},\quad W_{B,\text{K}}^{(l)}=U_{A,\text{K}}^{(l)}W_{B,\text{K}}^{(l)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.p4.1" class="ltx_p">On the other hand, semi-orthogonal <math id="A2.SS4.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{B,\text{Q}}^{(l)},U_{B,\text{K}}^{(l)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext>Q</mtext></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext>K</mtext></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{B,\text{Q}}^{(l)},U_{B,\text{K}}^{(l)}</annotation></semantics></math> are also possible. This is because of the common practice in pruning may select different different rows of Q,K matrices, which suggests multiplying Q,K matrices with row-wise partial permutations.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Next, we show how <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem2" title="Proposition 4.2 (Proof in Appendix ). ‣ 4.2 Residual Connections: Passing Manipulations Forward ‣ 4 Manipulations on An Open-Source LLM ‣ AWM: Accurate Weight-Matrix Fingerprint for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Proposition 4.2</span></a> is satisfied at the self-attention mechanism based on <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem4" title="Theorem 4.4. ‣ 4.4 RoPE and Attention Scores: Boundaries for Q/K Manipulations ‣ 4 Manipulations on An Open-Source LLM ‣ AWM: Accurate Weight-Matrix Fingerprint for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem 4.4</span></a>.</span> Let <math id="A2.SS4.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{B,\text{V}}^{(l)}=W_{A,\text{V}}^{(l)}PD" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext>V</mtext></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext>V</mtext></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{B,\text{V}}^{(l)}=W_{A,\text{V}}^{(l)}PD</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS4.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{B,\text{O}}^{(l)}=D^{\top}P^{\top}W_{A,\text{O}}^{(l)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext>O</mtext></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>D</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext>O</mtext></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{B,\text{O}}^{(l)}=D^{\top}P^{\top}W_{A,\text{O}}^{(l)}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then,</p>
<table id="A2.EGx10" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex38"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle X^{\prime}W_{B,\text{V}}^{(l)\top}W_{B,\text{O}}^{(l)\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext>V</mtext></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em">⊤</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext>O</mtext></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em">⊤</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle X^{\prime}W_{B,\text{V}}^{(l)\top}W_{B,\text{O}}^{(l)\top}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex38.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=cXPD\cdot D^{\top}P^{\top}W_{A,\text{V}}^{(l)\top}W_{A,\text{O}}^{(l)\top}PD" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext>V</mtext></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em">⊤</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext>O</mtext></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em">⊤</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=cXPD\cdot D^{\top}P^{\top}W_{A,\text{V}}^{(l)\top}W_{A,\text{O}}^{(l)\top}PD</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex39"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=XW_{A,\text{V}}^{(l)\top}W_{A,\text{O}}^{(l)\top}\cdot cPD" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext>V</mtext></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em">⊤</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext>O</mtext></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em">⊤</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=XW_{A,\text{V}}^{(l)\top}W_{A,\text{O}}^{(l)\top}\cdot cPD</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.p5.2" class="ltx_p">recovers the manipulation over inputs in <a href="#A1.E7" title="Equation 7 ‣ Definition A.2 (Self-Attention with RoPE). ‣ Functions ‣ A.1 LLM Architecture ‣ Appendix A Definitions and Notations ‣ AWM: Accurate Weight-Matrix Fingerprint for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Equation 7</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.5 </span>How Potential Attacks in <a href="#S4.SS5" title="4.5 Potential Attacks ‣ 4 Manipulations on An Open-Source LLM ‣ AWM: Accurate Weight-Matrix Fingerprint for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section 4.5</span></a> Recovers the Output of Transformers</h3>

<div id="A2.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We provide an illustration based on <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem3" title="Definition A.3 (Feed-forward Networks). ‣ Functions ‣ A.1 LLM Architecture ‣ Appendix A Definitions and Notations ‣ AWM: Accurate Weight-Matrix Fingerprint for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Definition A.3</span></a>, <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem4" title="Definition A.4 (Transformer Block). ‣ Functions ‣ A.1 LLM Architecture ‣ Appendix A Definitions and Notations ‣ AWM: Accurate Weight-Matrix Fingerprint for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Definition A.4</span></a> and <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem5" title="Definition A.5 (LLM Architecture). ‣ Functions ‣ A.1 LLM Architecture ‣ Appendix A Definitions and Notations ‣ AWM: Accurate Weight-Matrix Fingerprint for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Definition A.5</span></a>. Previous parts have demonstrated how the manipulations on inputs pass through self-attention. Hence, it suffices to show how the manipulations pass through FFN and yield an output identical to model A after the language model head.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS5.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS5.p2.1" class="ltx_p">For layer <math id="A2.SS5.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>l</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="A2.SS5.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{B,\text{gate}}^{(l)}=c^{-1}W_{A,\text{gate}}^{(l)}PD,W_{B,\text{gate}}^{(l)}=c^{-1}W_{A,\text{gate}}^{(l)}PD,W_{B,\text{down}}^{(l)}=cD^{\top}P^{\top}W_{A,\text{down}}^{(l)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext>gate</mtext></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>c</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext>gate</mtext></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext>gate</mtext></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>c</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext>gate</mtext></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext>down</mtext></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext>down</mtext></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{B,\text{gate}}^{(l)}=c^{-1}W_{A,\text{gate}}^{(l)}PD,W_{B,\text{gate}}^{(l)}=c^{-1}W_{A,\text{gate}}^{(l)}PD,W_{B,\text{down}}^{(l)}=cD^{\top}P^{\top}W_{A,\text{down}}^{(l)}</annotation></semantics></math>. We denote <math id="A2.SS5.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X^{\prime}=cXPD" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X^{\prime}=cXPD</annotation></semantics></math> as the manipulated input. Then for model B,</p>
<table id="A2.EGx11" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex40"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle f^{(l)}_{\text{ffn}}(X^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mtext>ffn</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle f^{(l)}_{\text{ffn}}(X^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex41"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\Big(\text{SiLU}\big(X^{\prime}{W^{(l)\top}_{B,\text{gate}}}\big)\odot\big(X^{\prime}{W^{(l)\top}_{B,\text{up}}}\big)\Big){W^{(l)\top}_{B,\text{down}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext>SiLU</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext>gate</mtext></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em">⊤</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext>up</mtext></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em">⊤</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext>down</mtext></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em">⊤</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\Big(\text{SiLU}\big(X^{\prime}{W^{(l)\top}_{B,\text{gate}}}\big)\odot\big(X^{\prime}{W^{(l)\top}_{B,\text{up}}}\big)\Big){W^{(l)\top}_{B,\text{down}}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex42"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\Big(\text{SiLU}\big(cXPD\cdot D^{\top}P^{\top}W^{(l)\top}_{A,\text{gate}}\cdot c^{-1}\big)\odot\big(cXPD\cdot{D^{\top}P^{\top}W^{(l)\top}_{A,\text{up}}\cdot c^{-1}}\big)\Big){W^{(l)\top}_{B,\text{down}}}\cdot cPD" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext>SiLU</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext>gate</mtext></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em">⊤</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>c</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext>up</mtext></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em">⊤</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>c</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext>down</mtext></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em">⊤</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\Big(\text{SiLU}\big(cXPD\cdot D^{\top}P^{\top}W^{(l)\top}_{A,\text{gate}}\cdot c^{-1}\big)\odot\big(cXPD\cdot{D^{\top}P^{\top}W^{(l)\top}_{A,\text{up}}\cdot c^{-1}}\big)\Big){W^{(l)\top}_{B,\text{down}}}\cdot cPD</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex43"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\Big(\text{SiLU}\big(X{W^{(l)\top}_{A,\text{gate}}}\big)\odot\big(X{W^{(l)\top}_{A,\text{up}}}\big)\Big){W^{(l)\top}_{A,\text{down}}}\cdot cPD." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext>SiLU</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext>gate</mtext></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em">⊤</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext>up</mtext></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em">⊤</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext>down</mtext></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em">⊤</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\Big(\text{SiLU}\big(X{W^{(l)\top}_{A,\text{gate}}}\big)\odot\big(X{W^{(l)\top}_{A,\text{up}}}\big)\Big){W^{(l)\top}_{A,\text{down}}}\cdot cPD.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS5.p2.2" class="ltx_p">By <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem4" title="Definition A.4 (Transformer Block). ‣ Functions ‣ A.1 LLM Architecture ‣ Appendix A Definitions and Notations ‣ AWM: Accurate Weight-Matrix Fingerprint for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Definition A.4</span></a> and <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem5" title="Definition A.5 (LLM Architecture). ‣ Functions ‣ A.1 LLM Architecture ‣ Appendix A Definitions and Notations ‣ AWM: Accurate Weight-Matrix Fingerprint for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Definition A.5</span></a>, the manipulation is propagated through transformer layers. At the language model head, we denote <math id="A2.SS5.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{B,\text{lm}}=c^{-1}W_{A,\text{lm}}PD" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext>lm</mtext></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>c</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext>lm</mtext></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{B,\text{lm}}=c^{-1}W_{A,\text{lm}}PD</annotation></semantics></math> and abuse <math id="A2.SS5.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X^{\prime}=cXPD" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X^{\prime}=cXPD</annotation></semantics></math> as the manipulated input. Then,</p>
<table id="A2.EGx12" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex44"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex44.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle X^{\prime}W_{B,\text{lm}}^{(l)\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext>lm</mtext></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em">⊤</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle X^{\prime}W_{B,\text{lm}}^{(l)\top}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex44.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=cXPD\cdot D^{\top}P^{\top}W_{A,\text{lm}}^{(l)\top}\cdot c^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext>lm</mtext></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em">⊤</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>c</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=cXPD\cdot D^{\top}P^{\top}W_{A,\text{lm}}^{(l)\top}\cdot c^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex45"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=XW_{A,\text{lm}}^{(l)\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext>lm</mtext></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em">⊤</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=XW_{A,\text{lm}}^{(l)\top}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS5.p2.3" class="ltx_p">recovers the output of model A.</p>
</div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
